<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Khamag Mongol</h1><p class="st-meta">1130 CE – 1206 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The 12th-century confederation of Mongol clans in the Onon and Kherlen valleys, out of which Temüjin built the Mongol Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mongol clans of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onon-river">Onon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kherlen-river">Kherlen</a> river valleys in north-eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mongolia">Mongolia</a> united in the early 12th century under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabul-khan">Khabul Khan</a>, an ancestor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, who is said to have defied the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/jin-dynasty-1115-1234">Jin dynasty</a> (1115-1234). The name means 'All the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>'.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation was a loose alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borjigin">Borjigin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tayichiud">Tayichiud</a> and other clans, choosing khans at assemblies. Its second khan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambaghai">Ambaghai</a>, was handed over by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> to the Jin and executed; his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hotula-khan">Hotula Khan</a> fought the Tatars, but after him the khanship lapsed and clans feuded, as with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yesugei">Yesügei</a>, father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a>, and the Tayichiud.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a> gathered followers in the 1180s and was acclaimed khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, then defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/keraite-khanate">Keraites</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naiman-khanate">Naimans</a>. In 1206 an assembly on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onon-river">Onon</a> proclaimed him Genghis Khan, turning the confederation into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 1130 CE – 1206 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.19%;width:1.51%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1130 CE – 1206 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Khabul Khan, Ambaghai Khan, Hotula Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Mongol</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mongolia">Mongolia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khamag Mongol Ulus, Khamag Mongol confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1168&amp;focus=khamag-mongol" aria-label="Khamag Mongol on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7142 550 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khamag Mongol lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7559 780h0M7269 802h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7462 806h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7462 806h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mongolia. <a href="/atlas?year=1168&amp;focus=khamag-mongol">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
